\lispPackageChapter{chorus}

Load this package with \texttt{(ql:quickload :chorus)}. It reexports the
kernel language from \texttt{chorus/lang}, the high-level API from
\texttt{chorus/api}, and two driver variables from \texttt{chorus/driver-api}:
\texttt{*show-messages*} and \texttt{*sdk-not-found*}.

\texttt{*sdk-not-found*} is true when the CUDA driver library does not load.
Driver calls then signal \texttt{sdk-not-found-error}. On a current Mac the
driver does not load, so this is the state of a Chorus image there.

The packages below are the ones \texttt{chorus} is built from. Use them when
you want a narrower set of symbols than the reexport.
